            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0874" n="748" xml:id="pg748"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6733: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-11-06T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                                1925—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 6—7:56
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>477. Following is excerpt from telegram dated November 4, noon, received from
                    Swatow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Chen Chiung-ming forces retired from Swatow, October [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">November?</hi>] 2. An officials left yesterday.
                            Cantonese troops expected to arrive at any time; Cantonese flags have
                            been raised and the city may be regarded as in possession of Cantonese.
                            No disorder, American destroyer here.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
